Variable-type evaluation and activation-address semantics — 2026-10-16

Scope: the owner decisions of 2026-10-13; EvoIR specification 2.6.5.
No Core, EqSat, Lean, raw EvoIR frame-walk or native memory-safety extension.

typeof evaluates a variably modified expression once at its declaration or
cast. Bound captures and operand scope remain. Fixed sizeof, alignment and
type-compatibility queries do not execute a nested capture. A runtime VLA
sizeof sequences captures on its own expression path, including short-circuit
and nested sizeof. Compatible VLA pointer subtraction does not require the
same hidden capture ID; existing stride/provenance/lifetime checks remain.
Scope entry remains E2945. A dereference after VLA lifetime remains E3010.
Parameter captures execute at definition entry; ordinary and nested callback
prototypes do not execute them or leak hidden objects to file scope. Repeated
calls retain their own captured bounds when a later operand changes a parameter.

Both source activation-address builtins return null for unsigned-int depths
1..65535; zero keeps its existing meaning. Range checking follows conversion.
The result remains neither an ICE nor a C null pointer constant. Invalid
depths are E2913. No ancestor frame is read. This is the owner's target rule,
not a claim that GCC frame_address has the same rule on every target.

